# Copy to .env beside tests/, or to this project's root, or export these in
# your shell. NEVER put real keys in any other file. The tests never print
# key values.
#
# Local Supabase stack — `supabase start` / `supabase status` prints these.
# NOTE: this repo's supabase/config.toml uses the 544xx port block (another
# local project owns the defaults), so the API URL here is port 54421.
# On a stock setup it would be http://127.0.0.1:54321 — trust `supabase status`.
PILOT_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54421
# The "secret" key of the LOCAL stack (legacy name: service_role key).
PILOT_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=
# The "publishable" key of the LOCAL stack (legacy name: anon key).
PILOT_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Remote (hosted) targets are BLOCKED by default. To point at the hosted
# project you must set BOTH:
# PILOT_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
# PILOT_PROJECT_REF=your-project-ref-here
# and PILOT_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
#
# Hosted keys: Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API. Never paste them into
# any file that is not this gitignored .env, and never print them.